  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Show that $x=1$ and $x=-2$ are zeroes of $P(x)$, and use the sum or product of zeroes to find the other zero.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q8a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3-2x^2-5x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Other zero: $3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-2-5+6\\\\&=0\\\\P(-2)&=-8-8+10+6\\\\&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $1$ and $-2$ are zeroes. Let the other zero be $\\gamma$. Using the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2+\\gamma&=-\\frac{-2}{1}\\\\\\gamma&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^3+3x^2-3x-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Other zero: $-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2+3-3-2\\\\&=0\\\\P(-2)&=-16+12+6-2\\\\&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $1$ and $-2$ are zeroes. Let the other zero be $\\gamma$. Using the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2+\\gamma&=-\\frac32\\\\\\gamma&=-\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
